  "narrative": "All estimates are already signed to the registered direction. For feature_027 direction +1, a positive estimate means feature_027=1 has a higher, less negative CRISPR dependency score, i.e. weaker dependency. The dominant evidence is now feature_027/outcome_014. H70 has an enormous positive overall association, +0.796 [0.776, 0.816], far above any approximate 10% outcome-scale reference, so I accept it as a dataset-specific association and request independent validation because a magnitude this large could also reflect a batch/technical artifact. H80 shows the effect persists within feature_042=0, +0.797 [0.774, 0.820], so I accept that subgroup contrast as well. The specificity panel is mostly outcome_014-specific: H71 outcome_006 is +0.030 but imprecise; H72 outcome_007 is below its threshold and imprecise; H73 outcome_001 is small; H76 outcome_013 is +0.027, just around the approximate 10% reference with a statistically positive interval but a much lower bound well below clinical importance, so it remains active but unresolved; H75 outcome_012 is small and opposite, with upper bound below the approximate outcome_012 threshold, so I reject that registered positive/weaker-dependency direction; H77 outcome_004 is small and unresolved. The feature_027/feature_042 stratification is important for interpreting H38. H78 within feature_027=0 gives almost no feature_042/outcome_014 effect, -0.001 [-0.022, 0.019], while H79 within feature_027=1 is imprecise. H80 shows feature_027 remains huge when restricted to feature_042=0. This pattern strongly suggests the accepted unadjusted feature_042/outcome_014 association H38 may be largely compositional/confounded by feature_027 distribution rather than an independent feature_042 effect. I therefore keep H38 accepted only as a marginal dataset association, not a central predictor, and mark it deferred. H81 is infeasible because feature_042 has no comparator within feature_009 level_001. H82 and H83 remain unresolved; their feature_009 level contrasts are imprecise and may be related to feature_042/feature_027 structure. I request validation of H70 to test whether the extreme feature_027/outcome_014 weaker-dependency association replicates independently.",
  "research_notes": "Round 6 appraise update: Feature_027 is the central measured signal for outcome_014. H70 accepted overall +0.796; H80 accepted within feature_042=0 +0.797. This is weaker dependency for feature_027=1. The overall effect is outcome_014-dominant, with possible smaller association on outcome_013 H76 and imprecise outcome_006 H71. H75 outcome_012 is rejected for the positive/weaker-dependency direction because the interval upper bound is below the approximate 10% threshold. Feature_042 H38 remains an unadjusted accepted association but is demoted/deferred because conditional contrasts show little evidence within feature_027 strata while feature_027 remains huge within feature_042=0; H38 likely reflects feature_027 imbalance or proxy structure. Feature_009 proxy checks remain unresolved/infeasible. Validation requested for H70. Proposed follow-up tests feature_027 within feature_042=1 to complete the conditional structure. Do not promote H38, H61, H47, H20, or weak calibration controls unless feature_027 specificity and H70 validation clarify the landscape.",
